  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>Solve each system of equations to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson. Enter your answer as “(x,y)” in the space provided. If any coordinate is a non-integer, enter it in decimal format.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="9bc99444-8aaa-47fe-a206-b69c41414c38"><problem><para>
      <para>1. \( \left\{ \begin{array}{c l} –2x + 5y = –42\\ 7x + 2y = 30 \end{array}\right. \)</para>
    </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((0,15)\)</para><para>\((11,−4)\)</para><para>\((1,−8)\)</para><para>\((6,−6)\)</para></problem><solution><para>\((6,−6)\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is (6,−6).
      </para>
      <!-- BEGIN WORKED SOLUTION 1-->
      <para>\(- 2( –2x+5y=–42)=4x-10y=84 \)
        \(5(7x+2y=30)=35x+10y=150\)
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        \(\begin{array}{r}4x-10y&amp;=&amp;84
        \\35x+10y&amp;=&amp;150
        \\ \hline
        39x&amp;=&amp;234
        \\x&amp;=&amp;6
        \end{array}\)
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS WITH LINE-->
        <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
        \(\begin{array}{rcl}7x+8y&amp;=&amp;4
        \\7(6)+2y&amp;=&amp;30
        \\42+2y&amp;=&amp;30
        \\2y&amp;=&amp;-12
        \\y&amp;=&amp;-6
        \\\end{array}\)
        <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
        The solution is \((6,-6)\).
      </para>
      
      <!-- ENd WORKED SOLUTION 1-->
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
